\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {\fs19 \trowd \trgaph108\trleft-108\trbrdrh\brdrs\brdrw10 \trftsWidth1\trautofit1\trpaddl108\trpaddr108\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10 \cltxlrtb\clftsWidth1 
\cellx1969\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10 \cltxlrtb\clftsWidth3\clwWidth4151 \cellx6120\row }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 Gargoyles often appear to be winged stone statues, for they
 can perch indefinitely without moving and use this disguise to surprise their foes. They require no food, water, or air, but often eat their fallen foes out of fondness for inflicting pain. 
\par Gargoyles speak Common and Terran.
\par }{COMBAT
\par }{\fs20 Gargoyles either remain still, then suddenly attack, or dive onto their prey.
\par A gargoyle\rquote s natural weapons are treated as magic weapons for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.
\par }{\b\fs20 Freeze (Ex):}{\fs20  A gargoyle can hold itself so still it appears to be a statue. An observer must succeed on a DC 20 Spot check to notice the gargoyle is really alive.
\par }{\b\fs20 Skills:}{\fs20  Gargoyles have a +2 racial bonus on Hide, Listen, and Spot checks. *The Hide bonus increases by +8 when a gargoyle is concealed against a background of stone.
\par }{KAPOACINTH
\par }{\fs20 These cousins of the gargoyle have the aquatic subtype. They have a base land speed of 40 feet and a swim speed of 60 feet (no fly speed) and are found only in aquatic environments.
\par }{GARGOYLES AS CHARACTERS
\par }{\fs20 Gargoyle characters possess the following racial traits.
\par \emdash  +4 Strength, +4 Dexterity, +8 Constitution, \endash 4 Intelligence, \endash 4 Charisma.
\par \emdash Medium size.
\par \emdash A gargoyle\rquote s base land speed is 40 feet. It also has a fly speed of 60 feet (average).
\par \emdash Darkvision out to 60 feet.
\par \emdash Racial Hit Dice: A gargoyle begins with four levels of monstrous humanoid, which provide 4d8 Hit Dice, a base attack bonus of +4, and base saving throw bonuses of Fort +1, Ref +4, and Will +4.
\par \emdash Racial Skills: A gargoyle\rquote s monstrous humanoid levels give it skill points equal to 7 x \u-4064\'3f(2 + Int modifier). Its 
class skills are Hide, Listen, and Spot. A gargoyle has a +2 racial bonus on Hide, Listen, and Spot checks, and an additional +8 bonus on Hide checks when it is concealed against a background of stone.
\par \emdash Racial Feats: A gargoyle\rquote s monstrous humanoid levels give it two feats.
\par \emdash  +4 natural armor bonus.
\par \emdash Special Qualities (see above): Damage reduction 10/magic, freeze.
\par \emdash Automatic Languages: Common. Bonus Languages: Auran, Dwarven, Elven, Gnome, Halfling, Giant, Terran.
\par \emdash Favored Class: Fighter.
\par \emdash Level adjustment +5.
\par }
\pard 
\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 
Girallons are savage, magical cousins of the gorilla. When moving on the ground, a girallon walks on its legs and lower arms. An adult girallon is about 8 feet tall, broad-chested, and covered in thick, pure white fur. It weighs about 800 pounds.
\par }{COMBAT
\par }{\fs20 A 
solitary girallon usually conceals itself in the branches of a tree or under a pile of leaves and brush, with only its nose showing. When it spots or scents prey, it charges to the attack. A girallon picks up prey that is small enough to carry and withdra
ws, often vanishing into the trees before the victim\rquote s companions can do anything to retaliate. Against larger foes, a girallon seeks to tear a single opponent to bits as quickly as it can.
\par }{\b\fs20 Rend (Ex):}{\fs20  A girallon that hits with two or more claw attacks latches onto the opponent\rquote s body and tears the flesh. This attack automatically deals an extra 2d4+12 points of damage.
\par }{\b\fs20 Skills:}{\fs20  A girallon has a +8 racial bonus on Climb checks and can always choose to take 10 on a Climb check, even if rushed or threatened.
\par }{\fs36 
